        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    net_income = 1_200_000\n    roas = 0.045\n    op_cash_flow = 1_500_000\n    prev_op_cash_flow = 1_200_000\n    long_term_debt = 4_800_000\n    prev_long_term_debt = 5_000_000\n    current_ratio = 1.5\n    prev_current_ratio = 1.3\n    new_shares_issued = False\n    gross_margin = 0.38\n    prev_gross_margin = 0.35\n    asset_turnover = 1.2\n    prev_asset_turnover = 1.1\n\n    # Calculate the Piotroski score\n    score = sum([\n        net_income > 0,\n        roas > 0,\n        op_cash_flow > 0,\n        op_cash_flow > net_income,\n        long_term_debt < prev_long_term_debt,\n        current_ratio > prev_current_ratio,\n        not new_shares_issued,\n        gross_margin > prev_gross_margin,\n        asset_turnover > prev_asset_turnover,\n    ])\n\n    return score\n```",
